### The Law: Substitution of Constants

In arithmetic and algebra, a function whose every input is a constant is itself a constant. This is the **Principle of Substitution of Constants** — a foundational rule of algebra, present in every standard treatment from Euclid through to modern analysis.

$$f(a,b,c,d) = \frac{a \cdot b \cdot c}{d^2} \quad \text{is a constant if and only if } a, b, c, d \text{ are all constants.}$$

